<title>SOUTH AFRICA: M-Cell yr shr back in profit.</title>
<headline>M-Cell yr shr back in profit.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1997-06-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year ended March 31</p>
<p>			(million rand unless stated)</p>
<p>Shr, (cts)</p>
<p>    - headline		8.4	   vs 3.0 loss</p>
<p>    - attrib		  8.4	   vs 0.3 loss</p>
<p>    Attrib income	  41.3	   vs 1.1 loss</p>
<p>    Pre-tax		  56.1	   vs 6.6 loss</p>
<p>    Tax			14.8	   vs 3.3</p>
<p>    Finance income	  6.1	   vs 8.7</p>
<p>    Turnover		579.6	   vs 254.3</p>
<p>Full name: M-Cell Ltd</p>
<p>NOTE - The company's primary investment is a 29.5 percent interest in cellular phone network operator MTN Holdings (Pty) Ltd, which it said was well position for further expansion in the cellular phone subscriber base.</p>
<p>M-Cell declared and paid a maiden dividend of two cents a share on March 31 1997.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom +27 11 482 1003</p>
</text>
